# Use case 3 — the input is written by strangers, so the intake gate is a security control.

@meta
use_case: Inbound support messages grouped into cases, roughly 900 a week
author: Team 3
date: 2026-09-21
approver: D. Aluko, Support Duty Manager
exit_criterion: Shut down if misrouted cases exceeds 15 percent in any month

@assumptions
- Messages arrive with a thread identifier the mail system sets and does not reuse
- Customer tier is retrievable from the account system at ingest time
- Attachments are not read by this loop in its first version

@unit
definition: One case, being the set of messages about a single problem from one customer
kind: judgment
two_people_test: Two agents would disagree about whether two messages are one problem or two
checked_by: A deterministic coverage check confirms every selected message belongs to exactly one case; orphans go to a human
fanout: 3
fanout_reason: Bounded by what the duty manager reviews in one sitting, and a misroute is expensive to unwind

@steps
1 | ingest | mechanical | code | Pull unassigned inbound messages and strip signatures and quoted history | batch
2 | cluster | mechanical | code | Group messages by sender, thread identifier and subject into candidate cases | batch
3 | select | coordination | code | Order by age and customer tier, capped at the review budget | batch
4 | gate-intake | gate | code | Refuse messages carrying credentials or from senders that are not customers
5 | triage | thinking | model | Decide whether the messages are one case, and which product area owns it
6 | coverage | test | code | Confirm every selected message belongs to exactly one case and none is orphaned
7 | gate-routing | gate | code | Refuse when a message belongs to no case or to more than one
8 | prove | mechanical | code | Write the message list, the clustering, the coverage result and the routing, then checksum it
9 | deliver | coordination | code | Write a routing proposal assigned to the named approver

@gates
4 | the message contains an account credential, or the sender is not a known customer | Hand the message to the security desk and do not place its text into any downstream system
7 | a selected message belongs to no case, or to more than one | Return the batch to the duty manager and have a person assign the orphaned messages by hand
9 | proof checksum differs from the checksum recorded when it was written | Stop the routing and have the support owner establish who edited the proof and when

@evidence
writer_step: 8
artifact: The message identifiers, the clustering that produced the case, the coverage check, and the routing decision
integrity: SHA-256 recorded at write time and re-checked before routing

@record
transitions: memory/ledger.tsv, append-only, one line per transition, written by code only
units: memory/units.tsv, one row per ticket with its outcome and the deciding step
retention: 18 months
acceptance: memory/acceptances.tsv, SHA-256 chained, carrying the design digest and the signer

@kpis
cost per completed decision | cost | unmeasured
misrouted cases | quality | 12 percent last quarter
hours to first response | throughput | 9 hours
refusal rate at intake | control | not applicable before this loop
cases resolved per agent per shift | tvr-throughput | unmeasured
